---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import SetbackDivider from '../components/SetbackDivider.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About"
  description="The Setback is an independent research publication diagnosing the binding constraint behind America's housing shortage, city by city."
>
  <section class="section about-hero">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="eyebrow">About</p>
      <h1 class="about-hero__headline">Housing is simple until you look closely.</h1>
      <p class="standfirst">
        The Setback started from a frustration with how the housing debate
        gets flattened. Build more housing, everyone says. True, and yet the
        reason it isn't happening is different in every city.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <SetbackDivider />

  <section class="section about-body" data-reveal>
    <div class="container about-body__grid">
      <div class="about-body__main measure">
        <p>
          In Los Angeles, a project can wait the better part of a year for
          approval, and much of the city is zoned so only single-family
          homes are legal. That is a <strong>regulatory</strong> problem. In
          Detroit, there is no shortage of land or buildings, but investment
          does not flow to the places that need it, because the numbers do
          not work. That is a <strong>capital</strong> problem. In San
          Francisco, the land itself runs out. That is a
          <strong>structural</strong> problem. Same shortage, three
          different binding constraints.
        </p>
        <p>
          This publication takes one city at a time and asks a single
          question: what is actually stopping supply here? Each report runs
          the same measurements, walks through the constraint that governs
          that market, and ends with a development model that puts the
          diagnosis in dollars.
        </p>

        <h2 class="about-body__subhead">Who writes it</h2>
        <p>
          Zachary Boukkouri is a freshman at Colby College, from
          Bethesda, Maryland.
        </p>
        <p>
          He spent three years as a junior project manager at a family
          construction and development firm, where he filed the permits,
          tracked the budgets, and watched projects stall for reasons that
          had nothing to do with whether anyone wanted the housing built.
          That vantage point (closer to the job site than to the
          commentary) is what this publication tries to keep.
        </p>
        <p>
          The Setback is where construction, policy, and finance meet.
          Housing is the rare problem that none of the three explains on its
          own.
        </p>
      </div>

      <aside class="about-sidebar">
        <div class="sidebar-card">
          <p class="label sidebar-card__title">The Framework</p>
          <ul class="sidebar-card__list">
            <li><strong>Regulatory</strong>: the rules won't allow it</li>
            <li><strong>Capital</strong>: the money won't come</li>
            <li><strong>Structural</strong>: the place won't fit it</li>
          </ul>
          <a href="/#framework" class="mono sidebar-card__link">Read the framework →</a>
        </div>

        <div class="sidebar-card">
          <p class="label sidebar-card__title">Elsewhere</p>
          <ul class="sidebar-card__list sidebar-card__list--plain">
            <li><a href="/reports">City Reports</a></li>
            <li><a href="/calculator">Pro Forma Calculator</a></li>
            <li>
              <a href="https://x.com/thesetbackpub" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
                X
              </a>
            </li>
            <li>
              <a
                href="https://www.instagram.com/thesetbackpub/"
                target="_blank"
                rel="noopener noreferrer"
              >
                Instagram
              </a>
            </li>
            <li><span class="sidebar-card__placeholder">Substack: coming soon</span></li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </aside>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .about-hero__headline {
    margin-top: var(--space-3);
    max-width: 16ch;
  }

  .about-hero .standfirst {
    margin-top: var(--space-5);
  }

  .about-body__grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 320px;
    gap: var(--space-9);
    align-items: start;
  }

  @media (max-width: 900px) {
    .about-body__grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
  }

  .about-body__main p {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-5);
    color: var(--color-text-soft);
    font-size: 1.02rem;
  }

  .about-body__main strong {
    color: var(--color-text);
  }

  .about-body__subhead {
    margin-top: var(--space-8);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-4);
  }

  .about-sidebar {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-5);
    position: sticky;
    top: 100px;
  }

  .sidebar-card {
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    border-radius: 4px;
    padding: var(--space-5);
    background: var(--pure-paper);
  }

  .sidebar-card__title {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-4);
  }

  .sidebar-card__list {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-3);
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    color: var(--color-text-soft);
  }

  .sidebar-card__list--plain a {
    text-decoration: none;
    color: var(--color-text);
  }

  .sidebar-card__list--plain a:hover {
    color: var(--color-accent-deep);
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-underline-offset: 3px;
  }

  .sidebar-card__placeholder {
    color: var(--color-muted);
  }

  .sidebar-card__link {
    display: inline-block;
    margin-top: var(--space-4);
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    color: var(--color-accent-deep);
    text-decoration: none;
  }

  .sidebar-card__link:hover {
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-underline-offset: 3px;
  }
</style>
